CM ============================================================
CM NEC-2 Model: 7-Element 2m Yagi-Uda Antenna
CM Document:    TM-HFTN-NEC-005
CM Author:      Merv Martin
CM Date:        2026-05-02
CM ============================================================
CM Description:
CM   7-element Yagi for 144.2 MHz (2m SSB/weak signal calling freq)
CM   Free-space model (no ground) — for gain/pattern evaluation.
CM
CM   Elements: 1 reflector + 1 driven + 5 directors = 7 total
CM   Boom length: ~1.2m
CM   Element material: aluminium tube, radius = 0.005m (10mm OD)
CM
CM   Element positions (along x-axis, boom axis):
CM     Reflector:  x = 0.000m, length = 1.042m (half = ±0.521m)
CM     Driven:     x = 0.125m, length = 0.960m (half = ±0.480m)
CM     Director 1: x = 0.250m, length = 0.905m (half = ±0.4525m)
CM     Director 2: x = 0.460m, length = 0.895m (half = ±0.4475m)
CM     Director 3: x = 0.670m, length = 0.890m (half = ±0.445m)
CM     Director 4: x = 0.940m, length = 0.885m (half = ±0.4425m)
CM     Director 5: x = 1.200m, length = 0.880m (half = ±0.440m)
CM
CM   All elements horizontal: y-axis (E-plane vertical)
CM   Boom along x-axis
CM   Free space (GE 0, GN -1)
CM
CM Expected performance:
CM   Gain: ~12 dBd (~14.1 dBi) forward
CM   F/B ratio: ~20-22 dB
CM   Feed impedance: ~25-28 ohms (use hairpin/beta match or folded dipole)
CM   3 dB beamwidth: ~50 deg E-plane, ~55 deg H-plane
CM   Boom length: 1.2m (4 wavelengths at 144 MHz)
CM --- GEOMETRY ---
CM Wavelength at 144.2 MHz: lambda = 300/144.2 = 2.081m
CM Element radius: 0.005m (10mm OD aluminium tube)
CM
CM GW  tag  nseg  x1       y1        z1    x2       y2       z2    radius
CM
CM Wire 1: Reflector (x = 0.000m)
CM
CM Wire 2: Driven element (x = 0.125m) — split at centre for feed
CM Left half: y = -0.480 to y = -0.001 (gap at centre)
CM Right half: y = +0.001 to y = +0.480
CM
CM Wire 4: Director 1 (x = 0.250m)
CM
CM Wire 5: Director 2 (x = 0.460m)
CM
CM Wire 6: Director 3 (x = 0.670m)
CM
CM Wire 7: Director 4 (x = 0.940m)
CM
CM Wire 8: Director 5 (x = 1.200m)
CM
CM Free space (no ground)
CM --- GROUND: none (free space) ---
CM --- EXCITATION ---
CM Source at last segment of wire 2 (left half of driven, near centre gap)
CM --- FREQUENCY ---
CM Single frequency: 144.2 MHz
CM --- CURRENT DISTRIBUTION ---
CM --- RADIATION PATTERNS ---
CM E-plane pattern (xz-plane, phi=90, theta 0-360 deg, step 2 deg)
CM theta=0=forward(+x), theta=90=broadside(+z)
CM H-plane pattern (xy-plane, theta=90=horizon, phi 0-360 deg, step 2 deg)
CM ============================================================
CM YAGI DESIGN NOTES:
CM
CM Element tuning rationale:
CM   Reflector:  slightly longer than driven (resonates below f)
CM               Acts as a mirror; spacing ~0.15-0.25 lambda
CM   Driven:     resonant or slightly short; matched to feed
CM               0.125m from reflector = ~0.060 lambda spacing
CM   Directors:  progressively shorter (resonates above f)
CM               Increasing boom spacing as gain increases
CM
CM Segment count:
CM   21 segments per parasitic element = 0.0497m per segment
CM   11 segments per driven half = ~0.044m per segment
CM   At 144.2 MHz (lambda = 2.081m), segment = 0.024 lambda
CM   Well within NEC-2 guideline (< 0.1 lambda per segment)
CM
CM Feed system options:
CM   Driven element impedance: ~25-28 ohms (real, near resonance)
CM   Option A: Hairpin/beta match — add shunt inductor across feed
CM     Ltap ≈ 60-80 nH (short wire loop across feedpoint)
CM     Transforms 25 ohm to 50 ohm with proper inductive tuning
CM   Option B: Folded dipole driven element
CM     Transforms impedance × 4 (25 → 100 ohm) then use
CM     quarter-wave balun transformer 100:50 ohm
CM   Option C: Direct feed to 75-ohm cable (close enough for VHF)
CM
CM Boom correction:
CM   Physical elements on aluminium boom require shorting by ~2-3%
CM   of element half-length to correct for boom interaction.
CM   These NEC-2 dimensions assume isolated elements (or
CM   non-conductive fibreglass boom).
CM   For aluminium boom: subtract ~5mm from each element half.
CM
CM EXPECTED PATTERN SUMMARY:
CM   Forward gain:         ~14.1 dBi (~12.0 dBd) free space
CM   Backward gain (180):  ~-8 dBi → F/B = ~22 dB
CM   3 dB beamwidth (E):   ~52 degrees
CM   3 dB beamwidth (H):   ~57 degrees
CM   First sidelobe (E):   ~-14 dB relative to main lobe
CM
CM FIELD USE NOTES:
CM   Mount horizontally for SSB/CW weak signal work (144.100-144.200)
CM   Mount vertically for FM (144.200-148.000 MHz)
CM   For satellite (mode J/V/U): circular polarisation preferred;
CM   use two crossed Yagis with 90-deg phase shift (turnstile Yagi).
